    affiliation: "Delft University of Technology"
title: "Billow: Minimum-energy structural modelling of soft, inflatable structures"
abstract: >-
  Billow solves for the static equilibrium of soft structures -- cables,
  frictionless pulleys, geometrically exact Timoshenko beams, inflatable tube
  constitutive laws and wrinkling membrane fabric -- by minimising one total
  potential energy with IPOPT. Posing wrinkling and slack as states of the
  minimiser, rather than branches a residual-form solve must be steered
  through, is what makes the formulation appropriate for soft-kite structures.
keywords:
  - Structural Mechanics
  - Energy Minimisation
  - Wrinkling
  - Tension Field Theory
  - Geometrically Exact Beam
  - Inflatable Structures
  - Airborne Wind Energy
  - Soft Kite
